Test-only TLS material for the mitmproxy fault-injection e2e.

Not a production secret.

- `mitmproxy-ca.crt` — CA the Connect worker trusts via `SSL_CERT_FILE`
- `mitmproxy.crt` / `mitmproxy.pem` — leaf for `mitmproxy` and `mitmproxy-subdomain`
  (`pem` is leaf + private key, which mitmproxy `--certs` expects)

Regenerate:

```
openssl req -x509 -newkey rsa:2048 -sha256 -days 3650 -nodes \
  -keyout ca.key -out mitmproxy-ca.crt \
  -subj "/CN=mitmproxy-e2e-ca" \
  -addext "basicConstraints=critical,CA:TRUE" \
  -addext "keyUsage=critical,keyCertSign,cRLSign"

openssl req -newkey rsa:2048 -sha256 -nodes \
  -keyout leaf.key -out leaf.csr \
  -subj "/CN=mitmproxy-e2e"

openssl x509 -req -in leaf.csr -CA mitmproxy-ca.crt -CAkey ca.key -CAcreateserial \
  -days 3650 -sha256 \
  -extfile <(printf "subjectAltName=DNS:mitmproxy,DNS:mitmproxy-subdomain\n") \
  -out mitmproxy.crt

cat mitmproxy.crt leaf.key > mitmproxy.pem
rm -f leaf.csr leaf.key ca.key mitmproxy-ca.srl mitmproxy.crt
```
